    "body": "This seems like such a bizarre edge case that IMO following the 2/3 behavior is the simplest path to convergence.\r\n\r\nOn a more technical level, requiring extra state-tracking so that implementations can restore state in this edge case also seems not worth it. (I assume the spec change you had in mind was tracking what the state of the input was during the legacy pre-activation behavior?)",
